{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook 05 — KMeans Clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal**: Find natural customer groups in our data using KMeans clustering.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What you'll learn:**\n",
    "- How KMeans works (the algorithm step by step)\n",
    "- How to pick K — Elbow method and Silhouette score\n",
    "- How to evaluate unsupervised models (no labels!)\n",
    "- Visualizing clusters in 2D PCA space\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score, davies_bouldin_score\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load PCA-reduced data\n",
    "X_pca = pd.read_csv('../data/customers_pca.csv').values\n",
    "X_2d  = pd.read_csv('../data/customers_pca_2d.csv').values  # for visualization\n",
    "df_raw = pd.read_csv('../data/customers_raw.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'PCA feature matrix for clustering: {X_pca.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## How KMeans Works\n",
    "\n",
    "KMeans is simple and effective:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Initialize**: Randomly place K centroids (cluster centers) in feature space\n",
    "2. **Assign**: Each data point joins its nearest centroid\n",
    "3. **Update**: Move each centroid to the mean of its assigned points\n",
    "4. **Repeat** steps 2-3 until centroids stop moving\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem**: How do we choose K (the number of clusters)?\n",
    "→ That's what the Elbow method and Silhouette score solve."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Elbow Method\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inertia** = sum of squared distances from each point to its cluster centroid.\n",
    "Lower inertia = tighter clusters.\n",
    "\n",
    "As K increases, inertia always decreases (more clusters = smaller groups = tighter).\n",
    "But at some point, the improvement becomes marginal — that's the \"elbow\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Pick K at the elbow point."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "k_range = range(2, 11)\n",
    "inertias = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for k in k_range:\n",
    "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "    km.fit(X_pca)\n",
    "    inertias.append(km.inertia_)\n",
    "    print(f'K={k}: inertia={km.inertia_:.0f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(list(k_range), inertias, marker='o', linewidth=2, color='steelblue')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Number of Clusters (K)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Inertia (sum of squared distances)')\n",
    "plt.title('Elbow Method — Finding Optimal K')\n",
    "plt.xticks(list(k_range))\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Silhouette Score\n",
    "\n",
    "The **silhouette score** measures how well-separated the clusters are.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each point it calculates:\n",
    "- **a**: average distance to other points in the same cluster\n",
    "- **b**: average distance to points in the nearest other cluster\n",
    "- **score = (b - a) / max(a, b)**\n",
    "\n",
    "Range: **-1 to +1**\n",
    "- Near +1 → point is well-matched to its cluster\n",
    "- Near 0 → point is on the boundary between clusters\n",
    "- Negative → point may be in the wrong cluster\n",
    "\n",
    "**Higher is better.** Pick K that maximizes the silhouette score."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "silhouette_scores = []\n",
    "db_scores = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for k in k_range:\n",
    "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "    labels = km.fit_predict(X_pca)\n",
    "    sil = silhouette_score(X_pca, labels)\n",
    "    db  = davies_bouldin_score(X_pca, labels)\n",
    "    silhouette_scores.append(sil)\n",
    "    db_scores.append(db)\n",
    "    print(f'K={k}: silhouette={sil:.3f}  davies-bouldin={db:.3f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].plot(list(k_range), silhouette_scores, marker='o', linewidth=2, color='coral')\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('K')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Silhouette Score')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Silhouette Score (higher = better)')\n",
    "axes[0].set_xticks(list(k_range))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Davies-Bouldin: lower is better\n",
    "axes[1].plot(list(k_range), db_scores, marker='o', linewidth=2, color='mediumpurple')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('K')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Davies-Bouldin Score')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Davies-Bouldin Score (lower = better)')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xticks(list(k_range))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Choose K and train final model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Choose K based on elbow + silhouette agreement\n",
    "# (We know the true answer is 4, but let the metrics guide us)\n",
    "best_k_sil = list(k_range)[np.argmax(silhouette_scores)]\n",
    "best_k_db  = list(k_range)[np.argmin(db_scores)]\n",
    "print(f'Best K by silhouette: {best_k_sil}')\n",
    "print(f'Best K by Davies-Bouldin: {best_k_db}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use 4 (aligns with our known archetypes and the metrics)\n",
    "K = 4\n",
    "print(f'\\nUsing K={K}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train final model\n",
    "# n_init=10 means run KMeans 10 times with different initializations, keep the best\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=K, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "cluster_labels = kmeans.fit_predict(X_pca)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add cluster labels to the original data\n",
    "df_raw['cluster'] = cluster_labels\n",
    "\n",
    "# Final scores\n",
    "final_sil = silhouette_score(X_pca, cluster_labels)\n",
    "final_db  = davies_bouldin_score(X_pca, cluster_labels)\n",
    "print(f'Final model (K={K}):')\n",
    "print(f'  Silhouette score: {final_sil:.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'  Davies-Bouldin:   {final_db:.3f}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Cluster sizes:')\n",
    "print(df_raw['cluster'].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Visualize clusters in 2D PCA space"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cluster_colors = ['#FF6B6B', '#4ECDC4', '#45B7D1', '#FFA07A']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left: clusters found by KMeans\n",
    "for c in range(K):\n",
    "    mask = cluster_labels == c\n",
    "    axes[0].scatter(X_2d[mask, 0], X_2d[mask, 1],\n",
    "                   c=cluster_colors[c], label=f'Cluster {c}',\n",
    "                   alpha=0.5, s=20)\n",
    "# Plot centroids in 2D (project them)\n",
    "pca_2d_model = __import__('joblib').load('../data/pca_model.pkl')\n",
    "# Note: centroids are in the multi-dim PCA space; for 2D viz we re-fit a quick 2D PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA as _PCA\n",
    "pca_viz = _PCA(n_components=2, random_state=42)\n",
    "pca_viz.fit(pd.read_csv('../data/customers_processed.csv').values)\n",
    "processed = pd.read_csv('../data/customers_processed.csv').values\n",
    "X_2d_viz = pca_viz.transform(processed)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f'KMeans Clusters (K={K})')\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('PC1')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('PC2')\n",
    "axes[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Right: true archetypes\n",
    "archetype_map = {'young_spender': 0, 'stable_saver': 1, 'high_earner': 2, 'debt_stressed': 3}\n",
    "archetype_colors_list = ['#FF6B6B', '#4ECDC4', '#45B7D1', '#FFA07A']\n",
    "\n",
    "for archetype, idx in archetype_map.items():\n",
    "    mask = df_raw['archetype'] == archetype\n",
    "    axes[1].scatter(X_2d[mask.values, 0], X_2d[mask.values, 1],\n",
    "                   c=archetype_colors_list[idx], label=archetype,\n",
    "                   alpha=0.5, s=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('True Archetypes (ground truth)')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('PC1')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('PC2')\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('KMeans vs True Archetypes in 2D PCA Space', fontsize=13)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — How well did we recover the archetypes?\n",
    "\n",
    "Since we secretly know the true archetypes, we can check if our clusters match them.\n",
    "In real projects you won't have this luxury — this is just for learning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Cross-tabulate cluster vs archetype\n",
    "ct = pd.crosstab(df_raw['cluster'], df_raw['archetype'])\n",
    "print('Cluster vs Archetype (how much overlap):')\n",
    "print(ct)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Each cluster is dominated by:')\n",
    "for cluster in ct.index:\n",
    "    dominant = ct.loc[cluster].idxmax()\n",
    "    pct = ct.loc[cluster, dominant] / ct.loc[cluster].sum() * 100\n",
    "    print(f'  Cluster {cluster} → {dominant} ({pct:.0f}%)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Save results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "df_raw.to_csv('../data/customers_clustered.csv', index=False)\n",
    "joblib.dump(kmeans, '../data/kmeans_model.pkl')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Saved:')\n",
    "print('  data/customers_clustered.csv — with cluster labels')\n",
    "print('  data/kmeans_model.pkl — trained KMeans model')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Checkpoint — What you learned\n",
    "\n",
    "| Concept | Key point |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| KMeans | Iterative centroid assignment + update |\n",
    "| Inertia | Lower = tighter clusters, but doesn't tell you the right K |\n",
    "| Elbow method | Look for the point of diminishing returns |\n",
    "| Silhouette score | Measures separation quality, range -1 to +1 |\n",
    "| Davies-Bouldin | Average similarity of each cluster to its most similar cluster |\n",
    "| n_init | Run multiple times to avoid bad random initialization |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next up: Notebook 06 — Cluster Analysis + Product Recommendation**\n",
    "We'll profile each cluster, give them human names, and build the product recommender."
   ]
  }
